{
  "slug": "dopamine",
  "name": "Dopamine",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Dopamine is a Claude Code hook plugin with two modes. In Degrade mode, it\nopens YouTube Shorts or Instagram Reels in a compact window next to your\nterminal while Claude handles your tasks — and auto-closes when the work is\ndone. In Progress mode, it detects what Claude is currently working on (React,\nPython, Docker, etc.) and opens a relevant best-practices article that stays\nopen for reading. Switch between guilt-free procrastination and passive\nlearning with a single command.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 command** and **3 hooks**.\n\n- **Commands** (1): `dopamine`\n- **Hooks** (3): `PreToolUse`, `Stop`, `SessionEnd`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install dopamine@claude-community` from `Teese999/Dopamine`.\n\nWatch Shorts while Claude works. Read articles while Claude codes.",
